<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <Authors>Fred Catellier-Poulin, Michael Jolin, Claudine Gagnon</Authors>
    <Company>CAUCA 9-1-1</Company>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</PackageProjectUrl>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Description>External-system authentication Wolverine HTTP endpoints (logon/refresh) for Cause.SecurityManagement.</Description>
    <Copyright>CAUCA 9-1-1 (c) 2025</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>Cause Security Management Wolverine ExternalSystem Cauca</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.7.0 — Adds a permission-based endpoint gate: [AdministratorOrUserWithPermission] and
[UserWithPermission], enabled with AddPermissionBasedAuthorization(). Includes a security
fix: MultiJwtClaimsTransformer no longer grants the Administrator role to principals with
no issuer claim, which previously affected certificate-authenticated external systems in
applications that do not configure Keycloak.

Behavior change in certificate authentication: when two or more active certificate-bound
ExternalSystem rows share one CertificateSubjectDn, the request now returns HTTP 500 with
an Error-level log naming the duplicated DN. It previously returned HTTP 401, which was
indistinguishable from a rejected certificate. Only this fault changes — every other
authentication outcome is unchanged, and nothing that previously failed can now succeed.
IExternalSystemRepository.GetByCertificateSubject can now throw
DuplicateCertificateSubjectException. Alerting keyed on 5xx will begin firing on this
condition, and the affected integration typically retries, so dedupe on
CertificateSubjectDn at the log aggregator rather than alerting per event.

All published packages must be upgraded together. See the README section on
permission-based endpoint authorization for supported registrations.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Version>10.7.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>10.7.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>10.7.0</FileVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="WolverineFx.Http" Version="6.25.*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Cause.SecurityManagement.Core\Cause.SecurityManagement.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
